CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* member of extended temporary: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* aggregate with reference member, direct: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* copy out: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
goto conversion keeps a temporary alive together with the temporary (or the
declared object) whose value holds its address.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18
accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
